      "writtenOn": "2026-05-06T18:18:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Just wondering: if the range exceeds the addressable space, `pkvm_pgtable_walk()` will simply not reach the end of this range, i.e. it will only walk until the end of the addressable space anyway? So nothing bad happens if we don\u0027t check this?\n\nSo this check is just to help catching caller bugs, not prevent misbehavior of `pkvm_pgtable_walk()` itself? And we define a contract that if the caller wants to just walk the entire pgtable, the caller is supposed to use precisely pkvm_pgtable_max_size(), not ULONG_MAX or whatever?\n\nBTW it seems that for the same reason, arithmetic overflow wouldn\u0027t happen either (so `end \u003e start` check is, again, just to help catching caller bugs)?",
      "revId": "1ab0cab9399364b80008fcd840667292c17dcbdb",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
