      "writtenOn": "2026-05-08T02:23:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah, at first I thought the range exceeds the addressable space may result in walking the page table from the beginning again, but this is not true. And a second thought is that, the caller send a range like this seems also abnormal. The similar to the overflow case (the overflow is actually already checked by the `_pgtable_walk()` in the for loop before this patch, although that check also serves the purpose to identify the end of the walk). But as you pointed out, neither case makes sense for the callers. Without this patch, the pgtable walk can silently success.",
      "parentUuid": "bb665e15_b6d65e01",
      "revId": "1ab0cab9399364b80008fcd840667292c17dcbdb",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
